# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Linux (Omarchy/Arch) is the primary development platform since Oct 2026, so the
# previous Windows-first policy (CRLF for *.cs/*.csproj/*.sln) produced constant
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" / "CRLF will be replaced by LF" churn and left files
# with mixed endings. `text=auto` still detects binary content automatically, and the
# explicit binary rules below are belt-and-braces. On Windows, `core.autocrlf=false`
# and modern editors (VS 2022, VS Code) handle LF without issue.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files (never converted, never diffed)
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.dll       binary
*.exe       binary
*.zip       binary
*.csv       binary
